From 265b4093d7a84a111091c5fbb2927015d0d9ab64 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephan Raj Ignatious Durairaj <signatio@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 09:48:32 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Agent: fix WDS backhaul VLAN tagging for MLD radios and MLO
 clients

On MLD-capable radios, a downstream repeater's 4addr/WDS backhaul
child interface (e.g. "wlan1_1.sta1") was never getting VLAN-tagged.
Without the VLAN trunk, DHCP never completed on the repeater and
onboarding/cloning stalled even though L2/backhaul association
itself succeeded.

Root causes fixed, in the order they occur along the association
path:

- The STA-role NL80211 HAL never handled hostapd's
  WDS-STA-INTERFACE-ADDED event for MLD radios, because
  get_vap_id_with_bss() only matches the bare radio name while
  available_vaps is keyed by the link-specific name
  ("<radio>_linkN"). Add a fallback that retries with each link
  suffix and, on a match, fixes up the interface name to the
  resolved link so downstream MLO detection uses the same name the
  vap_id was actually resolved against.

- WDS-iface-ready notifications were cached per client_mac only, so
  an MLO client with multiple affiliated links had each new
  notification overwrite the previous link's pending entry. Recache
  per (client_mac, bssid) so each affiliated link keeps its own
  pending notification until its association event releases it.

- bss.enabled is computed once, synchronously, during the one-shot
  autoconfig VAPS_LIST_UPDATE handshake, before an MLD/4addr backhaul
  BSS interface is necessarily up. Once frozen false, nothing ever
  re-evaluated it. Re-check it at client-association time and, if it
  flips true, re-trigger traffic separation for that BSS.

- For MLO clients, the association notification's top-level bssid is
  the AP MLD MAC per EasyMesh 17.2.6, not a per-link BSSID, so
  get_radio_by_mac() never finds it in AgentDB (which only stores
  per-link BSSIDs). Fall back to resolving the radio via one of the
  notification's affiliated-STA entries, which carry genuine per-link
  BSSIDs, and use that resolved bssid consistently for all downstream
  lookups (WDS cache release, bss.enabled re-check) since that's the
  same bssid the WDS-iface-ready path caches against.

- ap_manager can deliver the same association event twice (duplicate
  nl80211/hostapd control-socket delivery). The legacy and MLO
  association handlers unconditionally erased and re-emplaced the
  client record on every delivery, so a duplicate arriving right
  after the first would wipe a wds_iface_name that had just been set
  by the WDS-cache release on the first delivery, with no pending
  entry left to recover it. Skip the erase+re-emplace when the client
  is already associated to the same bssid.

Also included, found while tracing the traffic-separation path:

- Controller: always add the TrafficSeparationPolicy TLV (with zero
  SSIDs when disabled) instead of omitting it, so the Agent gets an
  explicit disable signal per EasyMesh 19.1.3 rather than treating a
  stale prior policy as still active.

- Agent: when a TS reset() finds the config/ports unchanged and skips
  the rebuild, still re-verify/persist bridge assignments, since a
  BSS's vap_type (e.g. GUEST) can resolve after the last apply even
  when nothing else about the TS config changed.

Signed-off-by: Stephan Raj Ignatious Durairaj <signatio@qti.qualcomm.com>
